The documents of this directory are read by the tests beside them.

Four of them are the templates LibreOffice ships, taken from the sources
of it as they are, under the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0:

  libreoffice-business-letter.ott  extras/source/templates/officorr/Modern_business_letter_serif
  libreoffice-cv.ott               extras/source/templates/personal/CV
  libreoffice-beehive.otp          extras/source/templates/presnt/Beehive
  libreoffice-bpmn.otg             extras/source/templates/draw/bpmn

  https://git.libreoffice.org/core/+/refs/heads/master/extras/source/templates/

The sources keep a template unpacked, one directory to a template, and the
build of LibreOffice zips it: these were zipped the same way, "mimetype"
first and stored rather than deflated. What they hold is what the
repository holds.

They are read by "OfficeDocumentsTests.js", which asks of each one what a
test of a document written here never asks: whether the library still
reads what an office writes.

"opendocument-v1.3-part3.odt" is the standard itself, as OASIS publishes
it, and is read by "OdfContainerTests.js" and "LayoutTests.js".
